# !! DO NOT TYPE A REAL VALUE INTO THIS FILE. It is committed and this repository is
# !! PUBLIC. The placeholders are deliberately not blank, so a value left unreplaced fails
# !! loudly at authentication instead of silently becoming an empty credential.
#
# TEMPLATE, committed. The real secret is .env.secret.mcp-gateway-google.encrypted, and
# that ciphertext is the only copy. It was committed holding these placeholders; write the
# real values with, from the repo root:
#
#   ./scripts/onepassword-secrets.mts edit apps/production/browser-chaperone/.env.secret.mcp-gateway-google
#
# Run it YOURSELF rather than asking the agent to, for the reason in
# ../olya/env.secret.google-workspace.example. Same three keys and formats as that file;
# docs/mcp-gateway.md in activescott/browser-chaperone ("The credential move") says which
# credential belongs here.
google_workspace_client_id=<REPLACE-ME-with-oauth-client-id>
google_workspace_client_secret=<REPLACE-ME-with-oauth-client-secret>
google_workspace_credentials_json=<REPLACE-ME-with-credential-json-single-line>
